ef "/athletes/12944"} "Hans von Blixen-Finecke, Jr."] " was in eighth place after the first day. The endurance phase often determines the eventing medals and it did in Stockholm, as Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12209"} "Petrus Kastenman"] " had the best score with +69.87 and moved into the lead, ahead of Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12348"} "August Lütke Westhues"] " and British rider " [:a {:href "/athletes/12994"} "Frank Weldon"] ". However, the competition was close and if anyone of those three faltered in the jumping, the gold medal could change hands. In the end, all three leaders had two faults in the jumping phase, for 20 penalty points, and there was no change in final standings, with Kastenman winning the gold medal, followed by Lütke Westhues and Weldon."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12209"} "Petrus Kastenman"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1192"} "Iluster"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "-66.53"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12348"} "August Lütke Westhues"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2521"} "Trux von Kamax"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "-84.87"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12994"} "Frank Weldon"]] [: